ly 9, 1936.","t_chg":"Rochester's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days have warmed.","p_chg":"Across 153 complete years: Rochester's average low shows no clear change: +0.05\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.00 to +0.11) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. Rochester's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.23\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.18 to +0.28), about +3.5\u00b0F since 1872. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.80\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.41 to +1.19) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.62\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.23 to +1.00). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 2 of 12 months. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Rochester's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.06 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 35.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 1873 (49.89 in); the driest, 1887 (20.30 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 4 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}